This repo is an audit toolkit. You don't run it against a GitHub URL directly. You clone the other repo onto your machine, install the agent into that clone, and run the audit from inside it. Here are the steps:

1. Install the prerequisites (once)

Claude Code, Python 3.9+ and Git Bash (install.sh is a bash script, so on Windows run it from Git Bash).
pip install --user openpyxl
2. Clone the repo you want to review


cd ~/Desktop
git clone https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>.git
3. Install the audit agent into that clone. Run this from this repo's folder:


cd ~/Desktop/Aws-Connect-agent
bash install.sh ~/Desktop/<repo>      # installs into that repo's .claude/
# or, once for every repo on your machine:
bash install.sh --user
4. Open Claude Code at the root of the cloned repo


cd ~/Desktop/<repo>
claude
In VS Code, you can instead open that folder and start Claude Code there.

5. Run the audit


/code-audit connect-chat
connect-chat is the Amazon Connect ChatJS checklist. If the other repo isn't an Amazon Connect chat app, first make your own pack by copying claude/code-audit/packs/_template/, then run /code-audit <your-pack>.

6. Read the results, which land in audit/ inside the cloned repo:

audit/findings.json
audit/connect-chat-audit-report.xlsx
You'll also get a summary in the chat with the counts, the go-live blockers and the items that need a manual check.

The audit only reads the code and never changes it, so cloning a repo you don't own is safe. Add audit/ to that repo's .gitignore if you don't want the reports committed.

